---
railroad-ebnf-beta
accTitle: Four artifact definitions for controlled skill evaluation
accDescr: Four railroad productions define a model as a parameterized predictor with a decoding configuration and context limit; an agent harness as the executable control plane over context, tools, state, permissions, loop, verification, and recovery; a skill as a reusable capability artifact with representation, trigger, procedure, optional tools, version, provenance, and lifecycle; and evaluation as a protocol over a versioned configuration, repetitions, oracle, budget, and evidence.
model = "parameterized predictor", "decoding configuration", "context limit" ;
agent_harness = "context", "tools", "state", "permissions", "loop", "verification", "recovery" ;
skill = "representation", "trigger", "procedure", [ "tools" ], "version", "provenance", "lifecycle" ;
evaluation = "versioned configuration", "repetitions", "oracle", "budget", "evidence" ;
